	title = {\enquote{Photograph others as if you were taking your own picture.}},
	abstract = {In his last movie, My Stills 1952/2002,1 which is a cinematic essay on stills photography, against the background of photographs in which he himself appears, David Perlov makes the following remark: \enquote{Photography---photograph others as if you were taking your own picture, [or taking a picture of] all of nature.} This assertion addresses at one and the same time both the spectator and Perlov himself, who was well aware of the invasive power of the photographic medium, and it hints at the requisite measure of caution and humility required of the photographer when he aims his camera at others. When he trains the camera upon himself, he himself experiences the trials and tribulations of exposure through photography.
},
